  "presentation": {
    "images": [],
    "plugin": {
      "description": "When a party member gets on a mount that supports more than 1 person and is close enough, you will automatically get on.\n\nThis plugin is in testing and will have one or more issues, laid out below:\n\n- You may need to right click on the driver once each time you start the game before the plugin will automount their mount. A fix is being investigated.\n\nPlease report issues/bugs and post suggestions on the Github website by clicking the globe icon.\n\nPlugin from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Aida-Enna/XIVPlugins/main/repo.json",
      "images": [],
      "nsfw": false,
      "official": false,
      "richCard": false,
      "richnessScore": 1571,
      "summary": "Automatically ride on other people's mounts!",
      "webEnriched": true
    },
    "projectRepository": "https://github.com/Aida-Enna/XIVPlugins",
    "schema": "omega.evidence.presentation.v1",
    "website": {
      "description": "A collection of plugins for Final Fantasy XIV",
      "homepage": "",
      "images": [],
      "links": [
        {
          "kind": "source",
          "label": "Source",
          "url": "https://github.com/Aida-Enna/XIVPlugins"
        }
      ],
      "omegaBannerUrl": "",
      "readmeExcerpt": "# Aida Enna's XIV Plugin Repo\n\nIf you want to use these plugins, add `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Aida-Enna/XIVPlugins/main/repo.json` to your Dalamud repo list. \n\nThese plugins (with the exception of Portrait Fixer which I made from scratch) were abandoned by their creators/maintainers - I've fixed them up and added new features to them. For their protection, their original author names are now omitted.\n\n## Auto Login\n\nAutomatically logs you into a specified character when the game first opens, and optionally reconnects you to the game (and notifies you) when you get disconnected.\n\n## Auto Pillion\n\nWhen a party member gets on a mount that supports more than 1 person and is close enough, you will automatically get on.\n\n## Macro Chain Redux\n\nA fork of the original macro chain, this re-adds support for running a macro inside of a macro.\n\n## Portrait Fixer\n\nWhen you click \"Update Gear Set\", this plugin will automatically update and save your portait to match your new glam.\n\n# Deprecated plugins\n\n## Food Check\n\nSee who is missing food buff at countdown start and optionally post to party/echo chat with a customizable message.\n\nThis is now a main repo plugin - You will need to delete the custom repo version (using the trash can icon) and then make sure testing builds is enabled (/xlsettings -> Experimental tab -> Receive plugin testing builds), and it should show up.",
      "title": "XIVPlugins",
      "url": "https://github.com/Aida-Enna/XIVPlugins"
    }
  },
